                <pb facs="0997" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg861"/>

                <head>No. 615.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merrill to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 24, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 173]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copies of the
                    correspondence between the British commissioner resident here and His Majesty’s
                    minister of foreign affairs relative to the harbor of Pearl River, and referred
                    to in my dispatch No. 169, of the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. W. Merrill.</hi></signed></closer>






